Subject: [PATCH] riscv: fix the hwprobe cpu_set argument type on bionic

cpuinfo_riscv_linux_decode_vendor_uarch_from_hwprobe() casts its cpu_set_t*
to unsigned long* before calling __riscv_hwprobe(). That matches the glibc
signature, but the whole C-library hwprobe path is guarded by #ifdef
__ANDROID__, and bionic declares:

  int __riscv_hwprobe(struct riscv_hwprobe* _Nonnull, size_t, size_t,
                      cpu_set_t* _Nullable, unsigned);

so the cast introduces the very mismatch it looks like it should prevent.
cpu_set already has the right type, coming straight from CPU_ALLOC().

Nobody had compiled this before: Chromium only built cpuinfo's riscv/linux
sources for is_linux || is_chromeos, so the Android-only branch was dead code
until android riscv64 was enabled. With Chromium M151's clang,
-Wincompatible-pointer-types is an error rather than a warning, and the build
fails with:

  riscv-hw.c:145:62: error: incompatible pointer types passing
  'unsigned long *' to parameter of type 'cpu_set_t * _Nullable'

Applied to the third_party/cpuinfo/src sub-repository (a separate DEPS
repository), not to chromium/src. Upstreamable to pytorch/cpuinfo as is.

Against cpuinfo revision ea6b9f1bb6e1, the one Chromium M151 pins.
---
 src/riscv/linux/riscv-hw.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/riscv/linux/riscv-hw.c b/src/riscv/linux/riscv-hw.c
index f67dc46bed34..75542e208786 100644
--- a/src/riscv/linux/riscv-hw.c
+++ b/src/riscv/linux/riscv-hw.c
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ void cpuinfo_riscv_linux_decode_vendor_uarch_from_hwprobe(
 	 */
 	int ret = syscall(NR_riscv_hwprobe, pairs, pairs_count, cpu_set_size, cpu_set, 0 /* flags */);
 #else
-	int ret = __riscv_hwprobe(pairs, pairs_count, cpu_set_size, (unsigned long*)cpu_set, 0 /* flags */);
+	int ret = __riscv_hwprobe(pairs, pairs_count, cpu_set_size, cpu_set, 0 /* flags */);
 #endif
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		cpuinfo_log_warning("failed to get hwprobe information, err: %d", ret);
